diff --git a/CHANGES.rst b/CHANGES.rst
index 5fee5f3..4c27a41 100644
--- a/CHANGES.rst
+++ b/CHANGES.rst
@@ -3,6 +3,11 @@
 Version 3.2.0
 -------------
 
+-   ``Response`` recognizes all ``Sequence`` bodies as buffered and all other
+    iterables as streamed, even if they have a length. Buffering closes the
+    original iterable immediately. Mixed string and bytes chunks, ``Response.stream``, and
+    setting ``automatically_set_content_length`` are deprecated and will be
+    removed in Werkzeug 4.0. Plain string and bytes bodies remain supported.
 -   Drop support for Python 3.9 and 3.10. :pr:`3098`
 -   Remove previous deprecated code: :pr:`3099`
 
diff --git a/docs/wrappers.rst b/docs/wrappers.rst
index 05d8066..873be4e 100644
--- a/docs/wrappers.rst
+++ b/docs/wrappers.rst
@@ -24,6 +24,30 @@ modify it multiple times. Set it to ``None`` or use ``del`` to unset the header.
 Each property below documents its type and what behaviors it has.
 
 
+Response Bodies
+---------------
+
+Pass a string or bytes to :class:`.Response` for a complete body. A string
+is encoded as UTF-8. For multiple chunks, pass an iterable of bytes or strings. A
+:class:`collections.abc.Sequence`, such as a list or tuple, is buffered and
+its content length can be calculated without consuming a stream. Other
+iterables are streamed, even if they define ``__len__``.
+
+:meth:`.Response.make_sequence` buffers and encodes the body, then immediately
+closes the original iterable if it has a ``close`` method. Accessing
+:attr:`.Response.data` can do this implicitly for streamed bodies.
+
+An iterable of strings is encoded as UTF-8. Mixing strings and bytes in one
+iterable is deprecated. Encode text chunks before yielding them when mixing.
+
+:attr:`.Response.stream` is deprecated. Write to an external buffer such as
+:class:`io.BytesIO`, then pass ``buffer.getvalue()`` to ``Response`` instead.
+Setting :attr:`.Response.automatically_set_content_length` is deprecated.
+Content length will always be calculated when possible without consuming a
+streaming body in Werkzeug 4.0. Set :attr:`.Response.content_length` explicitly
+when the length of a streamed body is known.
+
+
 Wrapping a WSGI Application
 ---------------------------
 
